      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Open the bean",
      "summary": "The opening half of every bean's life: check before you create, find out whose it is, and claim it before any work starts — or leave it alone when it is someone else's.",
      "description": "The opening half of every bean's life: check before you create, find out whose it is, and claim it before any work starts — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. Called, never run on its own: the caller is the process about to do the work, and it calls this where the bean becomes its own.\n\nThe caller's own gateway reads which end this reached. `Claimed` means the bean is in progress and the caller works it; `not yours` means a sibling holds it, nothing was written, and the caller stops. Process_BeanClose is the other half, called before each end the caller reaches after a claim.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
